				{
					id: "35F1AC955F5EBC8A"
					type: "xp"
					xp: 30
				}
			]
			subtitle: "But the kill was only the key. The way forward bends upward now — into the End’s abyss, where reality thins to nothing but obsidian and shrieking wind. There, coiled around a tower of cracked bedrock, waits the Draconic Voidlasher — a dragon warped by something older than dragons themselves. Its scales glisten with voidlight, its roar shreds the sky into static. The battle feels like clawing open your own ribcage. Each swing bounces off its armor until you slip beneath its wings, your Abyssal Axe singing, your boots scraping across floating stone. When the beast collapses, it vomits starlight and glassy shards — the Void Geode, pulsing in your palm like a cold second heart."
